class AccountHealthIssue(TypedDict):
    #: `ACCOUNT_REVOKED`: disconnected. `TOKEN_EXPIRED`: the platform login expired and Ampost cannot renew it. `MISSING_SCOPE:<scope>`: a permission needed to publish was not granted, e.g. `MISSING_SCOPE:w_member_social`. `REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRING`: the platform login (refresh token) ends within 7 days; after that the account needs a reconnect. `TOKEN_EXPIRING`: the token expires within 7 days and Ampost cannot renew it (no refresh token, or the platform refused the renewal); reconnect before then. `ACCOUNT_LIMIT_REACHED`: the account is beyond the plan's social account limit, so it cannot publish until the user disconnects others or upgrades (no reconnect needed). `PLATFORM_COMING_SOON`: the platform is coming soon and not open to this account yet, so it does not publish (no reconnect helps). `BOARD_NOT_SELECTED` (Pinterest, warning): the account has no default board, so every post needs `options.pinterest.boardId`; pick one with accounts_set_board (no reconnect needed).
    code: str
    #: `error`: the account cannot publish. `warning`: it can publish now but needs attention soon.
    severity: Literal["error", "warning"]
    #: What is wrong and what to do, safe to show to the user
    message: str


